Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer
6.Project Testing Phase
Testing is performed to verify that the flow correctly classifies different types of tickets.

6.1 Test Cases
Test Case	Input	Expected Result
TC01	"Forgot my password"	Access Issue / Service Desk
TC02	"Laptop screen not working"	Hardware Issue / Hardware Support
TC03	"Application is showing an error"	Software Issue / Application Support
TC04	"Office Wi-Fi is not working"	Network Issue / Network Support
TC05	"Email is not working"	Email Issue / Messaging Support
TC06	Unrecognized issue	General / Service Desk

6.2 Testing Objectives
The testing phase verifies:

Whether the trigger executes correctly.

Whether conditions identify the correct ticket type.

Whether the correct category is selected.

Whether the correct assignment group is selected.

Whether ticket fields are updated.

Whether unmatched tickets are handled correctly.

Whether the flow handles multiple ticket scenarios without errors.

6.3 Error Handling
If a ticket does not satisfy any classification condition, the flow should send it to a default category and support group rather than leaving the ticket without an assignment.

Example:

Unclassified Ticket → General Category → Service Desk
